multiflexi-executor (1.18.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix Kubernetes artifact collection: copy app_artifacts path patterns from
    pod /tmp into host MULTIFLEXI_TMP for Job::runEnd() (not FileStore)
  * Fix Kubernetes and Podman executor logo() data URIs with valid embedded SVG
    base64 (matches Docker executor pattern)
  * Install executor SVG icons under usr/share/multiflexi/images/ for the web UI
  * Improve Kubernetes executor for Helm-optional runs, quiet side commands, and
    MULTIFLEXI_K8S_NAMESPACE; add packaged RBAC manifest and deployment readme
  * Improve Docker executor with --rm env-file one-shot container runs

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0200

multiflexi-executor (1.18.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add Phase 2 credential availability gate before performJob(): checks each
    assigned credential via checkAvailability(), defers with retry for
    Unavailable/Degraded, blocks for Misconfigured; exits EX_TEMPFAIL (75)
  * Reports blocked jobs to SQL log, Zabbix, and OpenTelemetry via
    Job::reportCredentialBlocked()
  * fix: -t/--timeout was declared as a getopt optional-value option, so
    space-separated invocations like "-t 180" silently failed to parse and
    fell back to an unlimited wait (0). Changed to a required-value option
    so "-t 180" and "--timeout 180" are parsed correctly. Executor processes
    started with the old binary and no timeout could hang indefinitely
    waiting for a job that will never finish (e.g. after its Job row was
    cleaned up by `multiflexi queue:fix`); such stale processes must be
    killed manually after upgrading.

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200

